<title>TURKEY: Turkish May trade deficit up 89 percent yr-on-yr.</title>
<headline>Turkish May trade deficit up 89 percent yr-on-yr.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's foreign trade deficit rose by 89 percent in May to $2.042 billion from $1.08 billion in the same 1995 month, the State Institute of Statistics said.</p>
<p> TRADE (BLN DLRS)   May96    May95     Jan-May96    Jan-May95</p>
<p>Exports		 1.728    1.504	 9.002	  8.121</p>
<p>Imports		 3.770    2.584	16.789	 12.423</p>
<p>Trade Balance	-2.042   -1.080	-7.787	 -4.302</p>
<p>Note - Figures on customs-cleared basis and may not add up due to rounding.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
